2026-07-08 14:03:14,311 | AGENT | ProjectCoordinator Agent answered: Based on our company context, I can outline the key project milestones, timelines, and resource allocation requirements. Our hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure will be used. 

The project will start with the Framing phase, which will pay particular attention to confidentiality, existing production tools, and seasonality of workload, given that our client is a regional accounting and statutory audit firm. This phase will end with a formal review and a go/no-go decision.

Next, we will proceed with the Design phase, where we will define the solution's architecture and ensure it meets the requirements for real-time updates, notifications, and strict confidentiality obligations. Our past experience with a national professional order and a regional council will be leveraged to inform our design decisions.

Following the Design phase, we will conduct a Pilot phase, which aligns with the client's requirement for progressive deployment starting with a pilot in one office or mission line. This phase will be crucial in testing our solution, identifying potential issues, and making necessary adjustments before proceeding with the Generalisation phase.

The Generalisation phase will involve scaling up the solution to the rest of the offices or mission lines, ensuring that it is fully integrated with the client's production tools, including accounting production software, payroll software, and document management systems. Our partner, Ligeo Conseil, will be involved in this phase to ensure seamless integration.

Throughout the project, we will have a dedicated team consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead. Change-management and training resources will also be available to support the client's staff during the deployment and post-deployment phases.

Given our available capacity, we can confirm our ability to onboard this engagement within the proposed timeline. The budget of 220,000 euros over three years is acceptable, considering our standard pricing and the scope of work involved.

Our governance practices, including a joint steering committee, operational committee, RACI matrix, and documented escalation path, will ensure that the project is properly managed, and any issues are promptly addressed.

In terms of timelines, we anticipate the Framing phase to last around 2-4 weeks, the Design phase around 8-12 weeks, the Pilot phase around 12-16 weeks, and the Generalisation phase around 20-24 weeks. The Run phase will commence after the Generalisation phase is complete, ensuring that the solution is fully operational and supported.

Please note that these timelines are approximate and may vary depending on the complexity of the project and the client's availability for feedback and decision-making.
