2026-07-08 14:05:35,171 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-07-08 14:05:35,172 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security & Compliance officer at Faber IA, I can attest that our company has the necessary certifications and measures in place to comply with the client's requirements. 

We hold ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of our services, ensuring that we have a robust information security management system in place. Additionally, our ISO 27701 certification demonstrates our commitment to privacy information management.

To ensure confidentiality and security of client data, we implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. Our key management is handled through EU-based infrastructure, ensuring that sensitive data is protected. We also employ strict partitioning with logical isolation per client and per mission, as well as access controls to prevent any cross-client circulation of data.

Our system supports pseudonymisation and data minimisation, aligning with GDPR principles. We also have configurable retention policies aligned with legal archival obligations. Role-based access control (RBAC) and audit logging are in place to track every system output and access attempt.

As for reliability and traceability of outputs, our product Atelier is grounded in sources and provides retrieval traces and figure source linking. It supports internal quality control and statutory audit review, ensuring that all information can be traced back to its original source.

In terms of GDPR compliance, we have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and maintain a data processing register. Our data processing agreements (DPAs) are aligned with GDPR Article 28, ensuring that all data processing activities are compliant with the regulation.

Our secure software development life cycle (SDLC) includes code reviews, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external provider equivalent to CREST level. We also have a vulnerability management process in place with remediation SLAs based on severity, as well as an incident response plan that includes detection, notification, and remediation, including the 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow.

Given these measures, I am confident that our company can provide the necessary security controls to ensure compliance with the client's requirements regarding GDPR, confidentiality, security, professional secrecy, reliability, traceability, and audit capabilities.
